# Seeds for failure cases proptest has generated in the past. It is
# automatically read and these particular cases re-run before any
# novel cases are generated.
#
# It is recommended to check this file in to source control so that
# everyone who runs the test benefits from these saved cases.
#
# Provenance of the seed below: it was drawn while this oracle was being
# validated against a deliberately broken engine — `select_impact` was made to
# return no incoming references, i.e. the exact under-selection the module
# forbids. The seed shrank to the smallest input that catches it: one new note
# appearing where an existing reference was waiting for it. Keeping it means
# every run re-checks that case before generating anything novel.
cc 58ec420fb18125371dd229fcc711f082ffb9d8dc7d841c2053008b4143775c62 # shrinks to batches = [[Write { path: "Gamma.md", body: "# Heading\n\ntext ^block\n" }]]
#
# The two seeds below were drawn when the file tree joined the cache: each
# creates a note in a folder that did not exist and deletes the note again in
# the same batch, so the semantic snapshot is unmoved while the vault has
# genuinely gained an empty folder. They pin the rule that a tree-only change
# is still a generation, and that the oracle's own notion of "client-visible
# state" spans both axes.
cc 38ba089826bdf6a2499d57f53ed9448a2afd1522acd93ad9ec175fd8f0a00858 # shrinks to batches = [[Write { path: "Nested/Deep/Gamma.md", body: "# Heading\n\ntext ^block\n" }, Delete { path: "Nested/Deep/Gamma.md" }]]
